---
/**
 * ButtonGroup
 *
 * The layout wrapper for placing one or two action buttons together: a flex row
 * that gives its buttons a consistent gap and wraps on narrow viewports. Reach
 * for it wherever two buttons sit side by side; today that is a talk's
 * slides/video links in a card body (`EntryList`). A lone button is composed
 * bare, which is what the detail pages' back links do, and the page-header
 * panel's `cta` is a prop `Grid` lays out itself. It owns only the
 * grouping/layout; the buttons themselves are composed as slotted children, so
 * each picks its own `arrow`/`back`.
 *
 * @component
 * @slot default - The button(s) to lay out (one or two `<Button>`s).
 *
 * @example
 * ```astro
 * <Card href="/talks/x">
 *   ...
 *   <ButtonGroup>
 *     <Button href="https://slides.example" external>
 *       <Icon slot="icon" name="slides" />Slides
 *     </Button>
 *     <Button href="https://video.example" external>
 *       <Icon slot="icon" name="video" />Video
 *     </Button>
 *   </ButtonGroup>
 * </Card>
 * ```
 */
---

<div class="button-group">
  <slot />
</div>

<style>
  .button-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--grid-padding);
    margin-block-start: var(--grid-padding);
  }
</style>
